From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tom Englund <tomenglund26@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 16:45:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] nvidia-modeset: don't register a backlight for an internal
 panel muxed away

On laptops with a mux switched to the integrated GPU, RM still lists the
internal panel, so nvRmRegisterBacklight() registered nvidia_0 for a panel
the GPU doesn't drive. Writing it changes nothing but resumes the GPU from
RTD3 (2.8 s on the boot critical path through systemd-backlight, and on every
brightness change), next to the iGPU's real backlight.

Only consider internal displays that are connected, or that a dynamic mux can
switch to this GPU later. Decide that once per display: the core channel is
also reallocated on resume and console restore, when a powered off eDP panel
may not be reported as connected.

Fixes upstream issue 1413.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/nvidia-modeset/include/nvkms-types.h |  7 ++++++
 src/nvidia-modeset/src/nvkms-rm.c        | 29 +++++++++++++++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 35 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/nvidia-modeset/include/nvkms-types.h b/src/nvidia-modeset/include/nvkms-types.h
index 8311422e..d8c5cb38 100644
--- a/src/nvidia-modeset/include/nvkms-types.h
+++ b/src/nvidia-modeset/include/nvkms-types.h
@@ -2194,6 +2194,13 @@ typedef struct _NVDispEvoRec {
 
     struct nvkms_backlight_device *backlightDevice;
 
+    /*
+     * Internal displays that a backlight may be registered for, determined
+     * by the first nvRmRegisterBacklight() call; see there.
+     */
+    NvU32 backlightDisplayMask;
+    NvBool backlightDisplayMaskValid;
+
     /*
      * Per-API-head RG semaphore callback lists for vblank interrupts with
      * precise timestamp tracking. This uses RG (Raster Generator) semaphore
diff --git a/src/nvidia-modeset/src/nvkms-rm.c b/src/nvidia-modeset/src/nvkms-rm.c
index 62b80ea2..8a12852d 100644
--- a/src/nvidia-modeset/src/nvkms-rm.c
+++ b/src/nvidia-modeset/src/nvkms-rm.c
@@ -5921,8 +5921,35 @@ void nvRmRegisterBacklight(NVDispEvoRec *pDispEvo)
         return;
     }
 
+    /*
+     * On laptops with a mux switched to the integrated GPU, the internal
+     * panel is listed but not connected to this GPU: setting its "backlight"
+     * does nothing, but resumes the GPU from RTD3. Skip internal displays
+     * that aren't connected, unless a dynamic mux can switch them to this
+     * GPU later.
+     *
+     * This is only decided once: the core channel is also reallocated on
+     * resume and console restore, when an eDP panel that is powered off
+     * may not be reported as connected.
+     */
+    if (!pDispEvo->backlightDisplayMaskValid) {
+        const NVDpyIdList internalDpys =
+            nvNvU32ToDpyIdList(dispParams.availableInternalDisplaysMask);
+        const NVDpyIdList connectedDpys =
+            nvRmGetConnectedDpys(pDispEvo, internalDpys);
+        const NVDpyIdList muxDpys =
+            nvIntersectDpyIdListAndDpyIdList(GetValidMuxDpys(pDispEvo),
+                                             internalDpys);
+
+        pDispEvo->backlightDisplayMask =
+            nvDpyIdListToNvU32(nvAddDpyIdListToDpyIdList(connectedDpys,
+                                                         muxDpys));
+        pDispEvo->backlightDisplayMaskValid = TRUE;
+    }
+
     /* Find a display with a backlight */
-    displayMask = dispParams.availableInternalDisplaysMask;
+    displayMask = dispParams.availableInternalDisplaysMask &
+                  pDispEvo->backlightDisplayMask;
     for (; displayMask; displayMask &= ~LOWESTBIT(displayMask))
     {
         NV0073_CTRL_SPECIFIC_BACKLIGHT_BRIGHTNESS_PARAMS params = { 0 };
